{
  "name": "Weekly HERE Tile Usage Check",
  "description": "Every Friday at 7pm Edmonton: pull HERE raster tile usage from GoogleAPILog for the past week, compare vs the ~2,900/day August baseline, and send the owner a short summary.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 19 * * 5",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "America/Edmonton",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "weekly_here_tile_check",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.0"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "weekly_tile_check": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "Weekly HERE tile usage report (Friday evening check, agreed with owner Sep 11, 2026).\n\n1. Read the RxDeliver app (id 68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6) GoogleAPILog entity records for api_type 'Map Tiles (HERE)' covering the last 7 full days (Saturday through Friday).\n2. Sum metadata.call_count per day and compute the weekly total and the daily average.\n3. Compare against the ~2,900/day August pre-cache baseline and the ~950-1,050/day post-cache norm from the Sep 7-11 week.\n4. Flag any single-day spikes or unusually large fetch bursts (check whether they look like legit new-tile fetches from panning/zoom vs a cache regression).\n5. Report the results to the owner with broadcast_message. Keep the WhatsApp reply SHORT (owner uses text-to-speech; long replies get truncated): weekly total, daily average, % vs baseline, one line on anything unusual."
          },
          "x-base44": {
            "description": "Pull Map Tiles logs, compare vs baseline, brief the owner",
            "title": "Weekly HERE tile usage check"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}